ushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 25%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $9.99 to $33.77 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: P/E 36.9 vs 16.5, EV/EBITDA 15.9 vs 8.5 and P/FCF 33.4 vs 22.8 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 45% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.0% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 12 covering analysts target $47.33 on average, 51% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.35).","It runs a 42% gross margin and converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.52x.","ROE of 7% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 2.6% of revenue on R&D and 2.3% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.0x net debt to EBITDA ($626.5M of cash against $1.6B of debt), above the 1.5x gate.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.68).","Goodwill makes up 44% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.0% over 3 years and 6.6% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 100%).","At current returns, reinvesting 70% of profits supports about 4.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -1.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-1.2% trend).","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (2.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 13, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 6.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $17.9M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.4% (0.3% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 5,200 employees, each generates about $491K of revenue, 0.8x the Basic Materials median, and productivity has risen 10.6% a year.","That works out to $44K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.8M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $11K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":30,"head":"Watch: priced 65% above its $18.94 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $9.99\u2013$33.77 range.","pros":["12 analysts' mean target $47.33 (+51%)","12-1 month momentum +42%"],"cons":["Trades 65% above fair value of $18.94","ROIC 6.4% vs WACC 9.9%","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 36.9x vs sector 16.5x","EV/EBITDA 15.9x vs sector 8.5x"],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD","no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital","too few checks pass (conviction 30)"],"buy_below":16.1,"vc":{"base":18.94,"base_src":"dcf","bear":9.99,"bull":33.77,"alt_median":5.93,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.196,"dispersion":0.2515,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 220% above the other models' median ($5.93)","bull case is 3.4x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":16.4623,"ev_ebitda":8.463,"pfcf":22.7638,"pb":2.1738,"roic":0.0591,"gross_margin":0.256,"fcf_margin":0.052,"div_yield":0.0194}},"ticker":"ESI","date":"2026-11-06"}